// Go workspace — lets every go command run from the repo root (build, test, vet)
// without cd-ing into the module. Each module here is ALSO a standalone Go module:
// building from inside it works exactly the same.
//
// One module per dependency tree, on purpose. The core (mantlekeep-control) links only
// bbolt; every adapter module carries its own heavy client dependency, so a CVE — or a
// registry quarantine — in that tree can never block the core's build. An adapter
// depends on the core; the core depends on no adapter, and never will.
go 1.26.6

use (
	./mantlekeep-control // the core — generic engine, bbolt only
	./mantlekeep-kafka   // governed-grant adapter for Apache Kafka (franz-go)
)
